TOTK: a mesh primitive's index vector stored whole by one thread where the host asks for it (the job's "mesh":
{"whole_indices": 1}, MeshStage.WholeIndices). The entry point let thread n store index byte n, so a triangle's three
components came from three threads; AMD's Windows driver for RDNA 1 and 2 ("AMD proprietary shader compiler") loses
those stores and every mesh draw of OoT came out empty there (docs/oot-xlate.md). Without the field every
translation is as before.

